      "result": "All 21 checklist items have been tested and recorded — the run is complete.\n\n**Results: 16 PASS / 5 FAIL**\n\nThe core resume-building flows are solid: creating, editing all content areas, template switching, section reordering/visibility, live preview, duplication with full data isolation, renaming, search, and sorting all worked as specified.\n\n**Failures found:**\n\n1. **CS-11 — No persistence (most severe).** Neither localStorage nor sessionStorage is used; reloading wiped every created, renamed, edited and duplicated resume and resurrected a deleted one, reverting to the 3 seeded samples.\n2. **FT-19 — Date filtering entirely missing.** The dashboard offers only a title search box and a sort dropdown; no date or date-range control exists.\n3. **CS-9 — No date validation.** End dates before start dates and far-future dates are accepted silently in both experience and education, and render in the preview.\n4. **CS-21 — Rename validation missing.** The dashboard rename dialog *saves* a whitespace-only title (card renders blank); the editor header rename correctly reverts but gives no feedback either way.\n5. **CT-20 — Minimal template drops the summary heading.** Custom (and default) summary headings render in Modern and Classic but are omitted entirely in Minimal.",
